GOAL: redesign Mission Control (services/mission-control, Angular) so a judge understands a run in 10 seconds.
Read plans/plan-06-mission-control.md, plans/CONTRACTS.md (v1.3) and services/backend (GET /api/runs/:id/summary,
GET /api/runs/latest, the stream and report endpoints) first. Windows + Git Bash.
Use GET /api/runs/:id/summary as the main data source and keep live updates from /api/runs/:id/stream.
Do not change any backend behaviour or API; if the UI needs a field that the summary lacks, stop and tell me which.
Keep all existing tests passing and add component tests. No external CDNs or web fonts; no new UI libraries.

RUN PAGE, top to bottom:
1. Headline banner: summary.headline in large text; verdict badge (red "BLOCKED", amber "NEEDS REVIEW",
   green "PASSED — within tested scope", grey "Running…"); a small always-visible mode label ("Direct pipeline");
   ticket id and how the run started (Bob / git hook / manual).
2. Timeline stepper: Change → Impact → Proof → Fix → Approve → Verified. Each step shows its state
   (done / active / waiting / failed) and a one-line result, e.g. "3 files changed", "Billing reached via billing.line",
   "Test fails at InvoiceTaxCalculator.ts:8", "2 lines in 2 files", "Approved by <name>", "18 + 1 tests pass".
3. Impact map (inline SVG, no library): changed files (blue) → event "billing.line" → consumer files.
   The broken consumer is red and labelled "not in your diff". Built from the blast-radius path; readable at 1280×720.
4. Proof panel: test name, status, the failing line with ±3 lines of source and the hazard line highlighted,
   one sentence "why" from the summary, and a collapsible raw test output.
5. Fix panel: unified diff with +/− colouring, file headers and the changed-line count.
6. Approve card: approver name field, the hash (short, click to show the full value), a 10-minute expiry countdown,
   Approve and Reject buttons. Disabled with a clear reason when used, expired, or the run isn't awaiting approval.
   Use exactly the same API calls as now.
7. Verified card (after apply): proof test now passes, full-suite counts before/after, rescan clean,
   verdict reasons in plain English.
8. Actions: "Copy as merge-request comment" (copies summary.markdown, shows "Copied"), "Download report" (existing
   report endpoint).

